# uClibc-ng .config knobs this example depends on, on top of
#     make ARCH=microblaze defconfig
# Set CROSS_COMPILE=microblazeel-linux- and KERNEL_HEADERS on the make line,
# then `make oldconfig && make && make PREFIX=<dir> install`.

# microblazeel is little-endian; defconfig picks big.
ARCH_LITTLE_ENDIAN=y
# ARCH_BIG_ENDIAN is not set

# Debug info so the library's DWARF line table exists to symbolize against.
# DODEBUG builds the library at -O0 -g; UCLIBC_EXTRA_CFLAGS=-g also carries -g
# into paths DODEBUG does not. -O0 gives the cleanest line mapping for a demo;
# drop DODEBUG and keep only the -g for coverage of an -Os library.
DODEBUG=y
UCLIBC_EXTRA_CFLAGS="-g"

# Static only. The standalone microblazeel shared loader (ld-uClibc.so) fails
# to link -- its .S objects assemble little-endian but the ldso link defaults
# to microblaze big-endian emulation. Static libc.a is all this example needs.
# HAVE_SHARED is not set
